onfirmed:\n          type: boolean\n    SampleOperationResponse:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - permissions\n        - status\n        - message\n        - recordCount\n        - records\n      properties:\n        permissions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n        status:\n          type: string\n        message:\n          type: string\n        recordCount:\n          type: integer\n        records:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SampleRecord'\n\n\nDATA MODEL. Give \"dataModel\": the tables this plan sets up or changes, as the database will hold them. A person approves it as a diagram with the plan, the factory keeps it in contracts/data-model.yaml, and after every build the database the code creates is compared with it: a missing table, a different key or a different relation fails the task.\n- Each table: name, purpose (one line), and every column with its type (string, text, int, long, decimal, bool, date, datetime, time, uuid, json, enum), required (false when it may be empty), pk on the primary-key column(s), unique where no two rows may share the value, values for an enum.\n- A relation is a foreign key: \"references\" on the column that holds it, naming the table and column it points at (a primary key or a unique column of the same type), and onDelete where it matters. A many-to-many relation is its own table with a foreign key to each side. A key over several columns together goes in the table's \"uniques\".\n- Every table has a primary key. Use the names the code will use for the tables and columns.\n- Model what is stored, not what the API returns: a field worked out on each request has no column.\n- No task writes contracts/data-model.yaml: it is the factory's file. Put the entities, the database setup and any migration in the fileScope of the first task that uses each table.\n\nRepository map:\nApp.Api/AppDb.cs\n  class AppDb\nApp.Api/Program.cs\n  class Program\nApp.Api/SeedData.cs\n  class SeedData\n    void Run(AppDb db)\nApp.Tests/HealthTests.cs\n  class HealthTests\n    Task ApiIsUp()","tools":["read_file","search","repo_map"],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-1 (d1): Seed data is for initial setup; behavior for running SeedData.Run repeatedly when sample rows already exist is not specified.\",\n  \"ASM-1 (d2): Demo seeding is setup data for an initially empty database; behavior for rerunning Seed:Demo=true when demo rows already exist is unspecified and not required by this draft.\",\n  \"ASM-1 (d3): SeedData.Run behavior for sample rows already present after multiple Seed:Demo=true startups is assumed not to be a required repeat-startup behavior; the system starts empty and uses seed data for set-up.\"\n ],\n \"critic\": [\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-3.2 allows 1–3 seed rows per table, but REQ-4/AC-4.1 requires two or three, so a table seeded with one row passes REQ-3 and fails REQ-4 (and REQ-4 otherwise repeats REQ-3).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.3 lists every path with an /api prefix (e.g. POST /api/auth/sign-in, GET /api/sample-data), but the anchored contract declares /auth/sign-in and /sample-data, and no servers/base-path anchor backs the prefix, which contradicts I-1's 'exactly as it is written'.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.3 lists about 45 operations but only two contract anchors exist, so nothing anchors the list's paths or shows it covers 'every operation' in contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The contract operations POST /sample-data/load, /reset and /replace put demo data in at runtime, which conflicts with REQ-5's 'insert no demo rows' when Seed:Demo is false and with I-4's 'runs that file only when Seed:Demo is true', and the spec never reconciles them.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec never says what sample-data reset/replace do to non-demo operational rows, the test-only fixture account, or the pre-existing rows that REQ-2/Q-2 must preserve.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-2.1 needs application tables created in a database that already has an unrelated table, but the anchored startup uses EnsureCreated(), which does nothing when any table exists; the spec names no schema-initialization or migration mechanism and no upgrade path for databases EnsureCreated already built.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The EARS forbids changing 'any pre-existing database contents', while Q-2 only protects 'compatible' data; 'compatible' is never defined, nothing says what happens to incompatible pre-existing rows, and AC-2.5's 'pre-existing application row' cannot exist because AppDb has no entities today.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-2.2 and AC-2.4 are labelled level 'api' but check that 'the corresponding database row contains' values, which is a direct database check rather than a public API surface.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-5.2 and AC-5.3 assert a 'demo row count of zero', but no column or marker separates demo rows from other rows (the fixture account itself is a row), so the check cannot be observed or decided.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"With Seed:Demo=false outside tests, no contract operation or bootstrap step creates a first account or its permissions (only a test fixture is specified), so every protected operation is unreachable in a real deployment.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-3.1 calls every contract list operation with Seed:Demo=true, but most require authentication and no principal or seeded credentials are given for that scenario.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.2 only covers errors the contract declares, so failures it does not declare (e.g. an unknown lotId/itemId/eventId with no 404, or the database being unavailable) have no specified behaviour.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Nothing specifies what happens when ration proportions do not add up to 100% or an ingredient has no unit cost or dry-matter value.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-7.1 to AC-7.3 refer to 'movement quantities', 'cost fields' and 'nutritional fields', and AC-7.2 to lb units, with no contract anchor naming those fields or units.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec does not say whether PATCH /rations/{rationId} after feeding events have been recorded recalculates those past events' consumption and cost or leaves them as recorded.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-8.1 to AC-8.4 and AC-8.7 hardcode a 409 status, and AC-8.6 assumes a 'Voided' status, inventoryMovements and lotFeedTotals, none anchored to the contract; if createFeedingEvent declares a different status, the requirement breaks I-1.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No behaviour is defined for voiding an event that is already voided (risk of a double inventory reversal) or for PATCHing a voided event.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-9.1 to AC-9.6 require JSON null for adg, feedConversionRatio, costOfGain and projectedShipDate without showing the contract declares them nullable; if it does not, this conflicts with REQ-1's 'without deviation'.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-9.3 hedges on field names ('feedConversionRatio or fcr', 'costOfGain or costPerGain'), so the response schema it relies on is unanchored and unverified.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The EARS adds 'or no positive gain remains toward the target' (a lot at or above target weight gets no ship date), which goes beyond Q-5; Q-5 only covered zero Days on Feed and zero or negative ADG.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"rubric\": 4,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-2 requires persisting derived or cached values, but no rule says when time-dependent values (daysOnFeed, projectedShipDate) or values changed by new weights or feeding-event corrections/voids are recomputed, so stored metrics can go stale.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Applying the contract's security requirements is never stated to leave '/', '/openapi/v1.json' and '/swagger' anonymous, yet the health test and the factory's product page depend on those routes.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 7,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The Program.cs lines 8–9 anchor quote contains the redacted placeholder «SECRET_1» and so cannot match the source text exactly (spec-lint already flags this anchor as not matching the code).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Seeding 'each application