\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall implement every HTTP operation in contracts/openapi.yaml with its declared method, path, parameters, request and response schemas, security requirements, success and error statuses, and behavior, without deviation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A PostgreSQL database configured through the App connection string contains a compatible pre-existing row in an unrelated table and has no application tables.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The unrelated row remains unchanged, the required application tables exist, and the response reflects persisted application data.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts, initializes its database structures, and a contract operation reads or changes application data.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A contract operation creates or changes application data, including a value differing from the existing value.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The corresponding database row contains the submitted values and derived or cached values returned in the response.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API completes the operation successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A successful API mutation has been committed to the configured PostgreSQL database.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response fields contain the committed values from the database row.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process restarts and a contract read operation retrieves that data.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A PostgreSQL test fixture contains an authorized principal established as test setup, an empty application-data state, and a contract operation valid for that principal that creates or changes an application record.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the saved value and a PostgreSQL row contains the same value.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client uses the contract operation and then reads the record through the corresponding API list or detail operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A PostgreSQL database configured through App with Seed:Demo=false contains a compatible pre-existing application row with known field values and a row in an unrelated table.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The compatible application row retains its original field values, the unrelated database row remains unchanged, and the response contains the retained application values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts and an authorized client reads the application record through its corresponding contract operation.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 8,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\")\\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_1»\")));\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 22,\n     \"lineStart\": 22,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall persist all application values its operations read or change, including derived or cached values used by later requests, in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string, make committed values available to later requests and after restart, and initialize required application structures without deleting or changing any pre-existing database contents.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A clean database is configured and Seed:Demo is true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response list count is at least one and the returned sample values include data drawn from contract examples.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts and a client requests each contract list operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The App database is empty and Seed:Demo is true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each application-data table contains 1–3 rows derived from contract examples, and the response lists show those sample values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts and database-backed list operations are requested.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 22,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 10,\n     \"lineStart\": 7,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true at application startup on an initially clean database, the Feedlot Operations API shall run App.Api/SeedData.cs to populate each application table with demo rows based on believable examples from contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A clean PostgreSQL database and application configuration Seed:Demo=true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each application table has two or three sample rows and each list response contains at least one corresponding row.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts and a test queries the application tables and calls their corresponding list API operations.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true on a clean database, the Feedlot Operations API shall populate each application table with two or three believable sample rows based on examples in contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Seed:Demo is false, the database has no operational or demo rows, and a test-only account fixture provisions a valid non-demo account with the contract-required authorization state directly in PostgreSQL, separately from demo seed data.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The protected list response statuses and fields conform to the contract without requiring a demo-seeded record.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client signs in using the fixture credentials and authenticates protected list requests with the returned authorization, including requests valid for an empty operational data state.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The App database has no operational or demo rows, Seed:Demo is false, and a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data provisions a principal with the permissions required by the protected lists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Every application-data table has a demo row count of zero, and the response lists contain no demo-seeded records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts, the client signs in with the fixture account, and the client requests database-backed protected lists using the returned authorization.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A clean PostgreSQL database, application configuration Seed:Demo=false, and a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data with the permissions required by protected list operations.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The demo-data row count is zero and the list responses contain no demo rows.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts, a client signs in with the fixture account and authenticates list API requests with the returned authorization, and a test queries the application tables.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 22,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 17,\n     \"lineStart\": 12,\n     \"path\": \"App.Tests/HealthTests.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    [Fact]\\n    public async Task ApiIsUp()\\n    {\\n        var res = await _factory.CreateClient().GetAsync(\\\"/\\\");\\n        Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.OK, res.StatusCode);\\n    }\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false at application startup, the Feedlot Operations API shall skip SeedData.Run and insert no demo rows, and serve contract operations without requiring demo seed rows, including protected list requests authenticated using a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The repository implementation is complete.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The review finds API and API documentation surfaces but no product-facing screens or frontend implementation.\",\n     \"when\": \"A person reviews its exposed web surfaces and frontend files.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API application built from this repository.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows API health or API documentation and does not show feedlot product screens.\",\n     \"when\": \"A person inspects its browser-accessible surfaces.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall expose only backend API and documentation surfaces, with no product-facing web application screens or frontend implementation in this repository.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A ration contains ingredients with stated proportions, different dry-matter percentages, and known unit costs.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response ingredient movement quantities and cost fields reflect the as-fed proportions and costs, while nutritional values reflect dry-matter values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client records a feeding event and reads the ration and event results.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A ration has two ingredients with known as-fed unit costs and dry-matter percentages, with proportions of 70% and 30%, and a feeding request delivers 100 lb.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response movement fields report 70 lb and 30 lb consumed, its cost fields equal the as-fed weighted cost, and its nutritional fields reflect the ingredients' dry-matter conversion.\",\n     \"when\": \"The feeding event is recorded successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A test-created ration whose ingredient proportions are percentages of as-fed weight, with different dry-matter percentages and known unit costs, and sufficient inventory.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response event shows each ingredient's consumed as-fed quantity and a cost equal to the sum of as-fed ingredient quantities multiplied by their unit costs, while nutrition values reflect dry-matter data.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client records a feeding event through POST /api/feeding-events.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a ration defines ingredient proportions, the Feedlot Operations API shall calculate ingredient consumption and ration cost from as-fed ingredient weights and use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An ingredient has less available inventory than a proposed feeding event requires and inventory and lot rollup values have been recorded.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the inv